## Output

{% if action == "validate" %}
Return ONLY a JSON object with this shape:

```json
{
  "valid": <boolean>,
  "issues": ["<specific problem>", "..."],
  "suggestions": ["<one-line fix>", "..."],
  "notes": "<brief explanation of the verdict>"
}
```

`valid` is `true` if and only if the supplied inputs are well-formed (names match the surface constraints, `agent_type` is one of the allowed values for agent surface, `mission` is concrete for swarm surface, `system_prompt` states role/inputs/outputs/constraints for agent surface, `agents` is a non-empty list of valid ids for swarm surface). `issues` lists each specific problem; `suggestions` lists a one-line fix per issue; `notes` carries any additional context. Do not include any text outside the JSON object.
{% else %}
Return ONLY a JSON object with keys: `name`, `agent_type`, `description`, `system_prompt`, `mission`, `agents`.

For each field, provide a suggested completion that would make the composition well-formed and effective, given the surface. If a field is already well-filled (non-empty and compliant), return an empty string for that key so the operator's supplied value is preserved. For `agents` (swarm surface), return a comma-separated string of suggested agent ids, or an empty string if the supplied roster is already adequate. Do not include any text outside the JSON object.

```json
{
  "name": "<suggested or empty>",
  "agent_type": "<suggested or empty>",
  "description": "<suggested or empty>",
  "system_prompt": "<suggested or empty>",
  "mission": "<suggested or empty>",
  "agents": "<comma-separated ids or empty>"
}
```
{% endif %}